# Paths and fragments that name nothing real BY DESIGN.
#
# One per line. A `docs/...` path here is exempt from check_source_doc_refs.py;
# a `path#fragment` entry is exempt from check_doc_links.py's anchor half.
#
# Legitimate entries: help-text examples, output destinations a run creates,
# test fixtures, template placeholders, in-app routes that look like anchors.
#
# NOT legitimate: a reference that broke when a plan was filed. Repoint it —
# the reference is prose that records why the code is shaped that way.
